# GitHub project board ids for vivek7405/pilots, project 10 ("Pilots").
#
# NO CREDENTIALS IN THIS FILE, EVER. It is committed, and this repo is public.
# What is here are Projects V2 NODE IDS: opaque object identifiers that grant
# nothing by themselves, the way an issue number or a repo id grants nothing.
# Every call that uses them still needs an authenticated token with project
# scope, which comes from `gh auth` and lives nowhere in the tree.
#
# The `.env` extension is the hazard: it reads like somewhere a token belongs.
# It is not. A token, a key, a webhook secret or an API password goes in the
# environment or in `/etc/pilots/`, never here.
#
# Source them rather than rediscovering them: Projects V2 is GraphQL-only and
# the budget is scored in points, so re-resolving four constants costs several
# round trips per run of any board skill. These never change.
#
#   source .claude/gh-ids.env
#
# To refresh if the board schema ever moves:
#   gh api graphql -f query='query{user(login:"vivek7405"){projectV2(number:10){
#     id field(name:"Status"){...on ProjectV2SingleSelectField{id options{id name}}}}}}'
#
# Read issues over REST (`gh api repos/vivek7405/pilots/issues/<N>`), which
# costs nothing from that budget. Reach a card's item id from the ISSUE node,
# never by dumping the whole board.

PROJECT_ID=PVT_kwHOAXW41M4Bh_Lz
STATUS_FIELD_ID=PVTSSF_lAHOAXW41M4Bh_Lzzhg4z4Q

